Functions in C instead
----------------------

These two come from libterae's own C, in src/port/generic, which
port_memmove.c and port_memcmp.c in this folder include. Nothing in them is
taken from elsewhere. Why there is no assembly for them:

memmove  The only permissively licensed assembly memmove found for 32-bit
         MIPS is NetBSD's common/lib/libc/arch/mips/string/bcopy.S, under
         the CMU-Mach licence. It stays out until a person confirms that
         licence for both of libterae's licences. It could not serve MIPS32
         release 6 in any case, because it uses lwl and lwr.

memcmp   No permissively licensed assembly memcmp exists for 32-bit MIPS.
         NetBSD's bcmp.S only tests for equality, and Android's last MIPS
         memcmp (2017) is C.
